{"title":"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three circles have radii <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> cm. If the mean (average) area of the three circles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/6/7e69c2a434170f325026480713c59a2a2596864f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30\\pi \\text{ cm}^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"17\" />, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/7/c27f2b2325abed35d8aefd210f13318ea674462a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 64 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 5 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 24 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 8 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"369\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of the areas would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/5/ea564c429f0177f4c2936e5aa087efc3edf8ba34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30\\pi \\text{ cm}^{2} \\times 3 = 90\\pi \\text{ cm}^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"184\" height=\"18\" /> because the average of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> areas is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/6/7e69c2a434170f325026480713c59a2a2596864f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30\\pi \\text{ cm}^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>The area of a circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/e/88e1ac9b59dc367092dad4ca13e35ab3442551ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi r^{2}$\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the radius of the circle, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/f/8df900b44d7c899e1a1e35ebb4d309e8eea197c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi \\times 1^{2} + \\pi \\times 5^{2} + \\pi \\times x^{2} = 90\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"250\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/5/175187267a0d74d3b52f4a5c4f38c8f801816ac7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi(1 + 25 + x^{2}) = \\pi \\times 90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"192\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39c49f6db29612a43844324622e41dc82300aafd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} + 26 = 90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/2/be282c22febbf08f0c0389b3a9f415efd7e01d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} = 90 - 26 = 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e6537b50bd1fb5a7a166bb8fa193de6341b25037.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\pm \\sqrt{64} = \\pm 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"131\" height=\"21\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> represents the radius of a circle, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/9/1a9aeb232e6697fdbcd2246f4fc2a0aa45a2c512.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"93\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_20\" titl